Description: Normalize builtin type display across supported mypy versions
Forwarded: no

The supported mypy1.19 JSON output qualifies builtin names (builtins.str, builtins.list) while upstream fixtures use short names. Normalize only standalone builtins qualifiers; retain exact type structure, user-defined namespaces, diagnostic line matching and every test.

--- a/oslo_versionedobjects/tests/test_mypy_integration.py
+++ b/oslo_versionedobjects/tests/test_mypy_integration.py
@@ -110,7 +110,10 @@
         self.assertNoErrors(messages)
 
         actual = {
-            m['line']: m['message']
+            # Mypy 1.19 qualifies builtins in JSON reveal_type notes;
+            # later releases display their short names. Normalize that
+            # spelling only, retaining container arguments and user types.
+            m['line']: re.sub(r'(?<![\w.])builtins\.', '', m['message'])
             for m in messages
             if m['severity'] == 'note'
             and m['line'] > 0
